Groundtrack — third-party notices

Project code: Apache-2.0; see LICENSE.
The original Dymaxion project's solar geometry, whole-pixel drawing helpers,
bitmap text renderer, and Dymaxion Draft glyphs are reused under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/huntrontrakkr/dymaxion-watch-face
Snapshot: 0eb59dfe52fa6838ad26a5621653edb6eab7d9f0 (0.5.3).
The new projection, trajectory cache, dither generator, and layout are original
work. Groundtrack is an independent project with no shared release identity.

Natural Earth 1:50m land data is public domain, distributed through world-atlas.
https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/
No live map tiles or map-service credentials are used.

Relief (public/relief.bin) is a quarter-degree grid resampled offline by
tools/generate-relief.mjs from the AWS Open Data Terrain Tiles (Tilezen Joerd,
terrarium encoding, zoom 3). At that zoom the tiles' source headers list only:
  Global ETOPO1 terrain data U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration
  (Amante and Eakins, 2009; not subject to copyright protection in the U.S.)
  GMTED2010 terrain data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey (public domain)
The grid is smoothed and generalized: not for navigation. No tiles are fetched
at runtime. https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md

Tracking-station positions (data/tracking-stations.json) are approximate, from
public histories of NASA's Mercury and Apollo Manned Space Flight Networks.
No NASA insignia or logotypes are used.

ISS fixture: historical June 2019 TLE from the Satellite.js README.
https://github.com/shashwatak/satellite-js
The fixture is not current telemetry and is restricted to its epoch in code.

Dithering was studied from Lucas Pope's Return of the Obra Dinn development log.
https://dukope.com/devlogs/obra-dinn/tig-32/
No game assets or implementation were copied. The deterministic periodic
void-and-cluster threshold tile is generated by tools/generate-dither.mjs.

Bundled runtime and offline geographic dependencies follow.


