Study 03 projection and city data
--------------------------------
The Gray–Fuller forward triangle transform in src/fuller.js is adapted from
Philippe Riviere's (2018) free/libre implementation, expressly dedicated to
the public domain (CC0) in his notebook:
https://observablehq.com/@fil/buckminster-fullers-triangle-transformation
The transformation implements the equations described by Robert W. Gray,
"Exact Transformation Equations For Fuller's World Map," Cartographica,
32(3), 1995. No source code from Gray's restricted implementation is used.
Icosahedral orientation follows Gray's published geographic coordinates.

The 243-place city catalog in data/cities.json is derived from Natural Earth
1:110m populated places, public-domain geographic data:
https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/blob/master/geojson/ne_110m_populated_places.geojson
https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/
Population values are used only to limit marker density, not as current estimates.

Study 04 art-direction reference
--------------------------------
docs/art-direction/shorelight-concept.png is an AI-generated material study
created with OpenAI's built-in image-generation tool on September 27, 2026.
The full prompt and context are in docs/art-direction/README.md. It is not
a watch screenshot and is not used by the map or watch renderer. Study 04
uses its own fixed 4x4 ordered color mixing; the older studies retain the
void-and-cluster screen credited above.


